The algebra starts from classical BFGS trace and determinant analysis,
associated with Powell~\cite{FND_P76} and Byrd--Nocedal~\cite{FND_BN89}
and developed in Nocedal's exposition~\cite[Section~5]{FND_N92}.

Recent global rate analyses also use matrix potentials, with distinct
Armijo--Wolfe~\cite{FND_JJM24AW} and exact-search~\cite{FND_JJM26EX}
results.
